    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d731">

                <pb facs="0877" n="869" sameAs="frus:frus1938v02/pg869"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">781.003/99</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Counselor of the Belgian Embassy</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Gruben</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Chief of the Division of Near Eastern
                        Affairs</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Murray</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">D7115 <lb/> No. 683</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-02-23">February 23, 1938</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Mr. Murray</hi>: With reference to our recent
                    conversation, I have the honor to send you herewith, for your personal
                    information, a memorandum setting forth the legal argumentation by which the <pb
                        facs="0878" n="870" xml:id="pg870"/> Belgian Government claims that the
                    customs régime of Morocco cannot be modified without its approval.</p>
                <p>This memorandum develops the considerations mentioned in paragraphs 2, 3 and 4 of
                    page 2 of the letter addressed by the Belgian Ambassador to the Honorable the
                    Secretary of State on the subject, under date of February 7th 1938.</p>
                <p>I remain [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Baron de Gruben</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d731-a1.xml" xpointer="d731-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
